# host-specific / regenerable — never bake into the image
_meta/.venv-online
_meta/.venv-embed
.git
.obsidian
.DS_Store
**/__pycache__
graphify-out
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# Proven NEVER read by the query-serving path (do_health/do_route/do_search/do_ask/do_page/do_expand/
# do_mcp_post) — deep-research RESEARCH 3: the only things `serve`/`ask`/`mcp` ever open are
# vault/reference/<domain>/, vault/{topics,entities,questions,outputs}/, and vault/taxonomy.md.
# Excluded from EVERY image's build context (root Dockerfile included, not just
# deploy/openshift/Containerfile) — smaller context, faster builds, and vault/_sources/ in particular
# (the hand-notes raw tier) never leaves disk.
# _meta/models and _meta/embeddings (the optional dense/hybrid layer) are DELIBERATELY NOT listed here:
# deploy/openshift/Containerfile's `dense` build target COPIES them explicitly, so they must stay
# available in the context; the root Dockerfile's `COPY .` also still picks them up for its full/online
# variant.
#
# Paths gained the `vault/` prefix on 2026-08-05 (content moved under one portable parent). Note
# vault/taxonomy.md and vault/.manifest.json are NOT excluded — they are vault DATA the serving and
# lint paths both require.
vault/_sources
vault/references
_meta/eval
_meta/tests
_meta/tkg
_meta/harvest

# The bind-mounted deployment supplies vault/ at run time (see .env.example / docker-compose.yml).
# Uncomment to build a slim, content-free image — PRODUCTION.md's "slim variant", where content
# updates never trigger an image rebuild. Leave commented for the self-contained/baked image.
# vault
